==French==

===Etymology===
{{rfscript|Gothic}}
From {{etyl|frm|fr}}, from {{etyl|fro|fr}} {{term|lesser|lang=fro}}, {{term|laisier||to let, let go, leave|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|LL.|fr}} {{term|lassare|lassāre|lang=la}}, present active infinitive of {{term|lasso|lassō|to let, let go, leave, grant|lang=la}}, partly from {{etyl|la|fr}} {{term|laxare|laxāre|lang=la}}, present active infinitive of {{term|laxo|laxō|to relax, loosen|lang=la}}; partly of {{etyl|gem|fr}} origin, from {{etyl|goh|fr}} {{term|lazzan|lāzzan|lang=goh}}, {{term|lazan|lāzan|to let, let go, leave||tr={{etyl|de|-}} {{term|lassen|lang=de}}|lang=goh}}, from {{proto|Germanic|lētanan|to let, leave, leave alone|lang=fr}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|lēy-||lēi-d-|to leave, let|lang=fr}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|lætan|lǣtan|to allow, let go, leave, rent|sc=Latinx|lang=ang}}, {{etyl|got|-}} {{term|||tr=lētan|to release, forgive|lang=got}}. Conflated also with {{etyl|fro|-}} {{term|laiier||to leave, abandon, allow|lang=fro}} (compare Old {{etyl|oc|-}} {{term|laihar|lang=oc}}, {{term|laiar||lang=oc}}, Old Northern {{etyl|it|-}} {{term|lagare||lang=it}}), from {{proto|Germanic|lagjanan|to lay|lang=fr}}. More at {{l|en|let}}, {{l|en|lay}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Fr-laisser.ogg|audio}}
* {{IPA|/lese/|/lɛse/|lang=fr}}, {{SAMPA|/le.se/}}

===Verb===
'''laisser'''

# {{transitive|lang=fr}} to [[leave]], leave alone
#: '''''Laissez''' le pistole sur le table''
#:: ''Leave the gun on the table''

